<div class="container">
    <div id="how-to" class="mission-statement scrollspy">
        <p class="grey-text text-darken-1"><strong>Regulatory reference:</strong> CYFSA, 2017, s. 74 (rights of children in care); O. Reg. 155/18, ss. 8 and 9 (complaints; review of complaints); O. Reg. 156/18, ss. 6 and 8 (policies and procedures; records and documentation).</p>
        <h2>Making a complaint</h2>
        <p>Complaints about a foster home or about Annie&rsquo;s Havens are taken seriously and the safety and well-being of the child is always paramount. A child or young person in foster care, their family, a placing agency, or a member of the community may make a complaint at any time. A complaint may be made verbally or in writing, in private or in the presence of others, and to any person the child feels comfortable with and trusts. Every complaint we receive is acknowledged within 24 hours.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card blue-grey lighten-5">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">support_agent</i>
                <span class="card-title">How to reach us</span>
            </div>
            <div class="row" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <div class="col s12 m6">
                    <p><i class="material-symbols-outlined tiny" aria-hidden="true">phone</i> <strong>(905) 294-2137</strong></p>
                    <p><i class="material-symbols-outlined tiny" aria-hidden="true">mail</i> <a href="mailto:alexis.mcneil@annieshavens.ca">Alexis McNeil, Compliance Manager</a></p>
                    <p><i class="material-symbols-outlined tiny" aria-hidden="true">mail</i> <a href="mailto:chriswilson@annieshavens.ca">Chris Wilson, Executive Director</a></p>
                    <p><a href="/contact-us">Use our contact form</a></p>
                </div>
                <div class="col s12 m6">
                    <p><i class="material-symbols-outlined tiny" aria-hidden="true">location_on</i> 517 Upper Sherman Ave.<br>Hamilton, Ontario&nbsp; L8V 3L7</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p>You may also bring a complaint to a foster parent, a Case Manager, the Program Supervisor, or any Annie&rsquo;s Havens staff member you trust. Anyone who receives a complaint will make sure it reaches the agency for action.</p>
            <p><strong>Ontario Ombudsman.</strong> A child in foster care has the right to speak privately with, and have visits from, the Ontario Ombudsman about a complaint. The Ombudsman can be reached at <a href="tel:18002631830">1-800-263-1830</a> or at <a href="https://www.ombudsman.on.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ombudsman.on.ca</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

