    <div id="rights" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">record_voice_over</i>
                <span class="card-title">Right to Make a Complaint</span>
            </div>
            <p>A child or young person in foster care has the right to make a complaint at any time regarding their care, treatment, or the actions or decisions of a foster parent, agency staff, or the agency itself.</p>
            <p>A complaint may be made:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>verbally or in writing;</li>
                <li>in private or in the presence of others; and</li>
                <li>to any person the child feels comfortable with and trusts.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This may include, but is not limited to:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>a foster parent;</li>
                <li>an agency staff member;</li>
                <li>a Case Manager;</li>
                <li>the Program Supervisor;</li>
                <li>the Executive Director; or</li>
                <li>a person designated by the agency.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>All individuals who receive a complaint are required to ensure the complaint is promptly communicated to the agency for action.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="overview" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">policy</i>
                <span class="card-title">Policy Overview</span>
            </div>
            <p>Complaints against the foster home and/or the agency or placing agency must be reported and taken seriously by all parties. The nature and severity of complaints may vary greatly and can come from many sources. Specific procedures are given depending on the source and nature of the complaint. At all times, the safety and well-being of the child is paramount.</p>
            <p>Verbal complaints must be documented and addressed in writing to the same criteria as written complaints &mdash; the complainant must at some point sign to verify a document outlining the complaint.</p>
            <p>The person who is the subject of the complaint cannot be the one to respond to the complaint.</p>
            <p>In all situations where there is a complaint against a foster home, it is the decision of the agency alone to close the home. The placing agency may wish to remove its children from the home; however, they cannot decide how the decision to close the home is ultimately handled. Where there is no protection concern and the complaint is easily addressed, all parties will seek to resolve the issue without further involvement of protective services.</p>
            <p>Records of complaints added to the foster home file will include:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>the circumstances of the complaint and possible investigation;</li>
                <li>who was involved;</li>
                <li>the way in which the investigation was conducted;</li>
                <li>the recommendation; and</li>
                <li>the action taken.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="requirements" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">rule</i>
                <span class="card-title">General Requirements</span>
            </div>
            <p>Verbal complaints must be documented and addressed using the same criteria as written complaints. Where appropriate, the complainant may be asked to sign a written record of the complaint. Where a child or young person is unable or unwilling to sign, documentation by the receiving staff member is sufficient.</p>
            <p>The person who is the subject of the complaint shall not be the person responsible for responding to or reviewing the complaint.</p>
            <p>In all situations where there is a complaint against a foster home, the decision to close a foster home rests solely with the agency. A placing agency may remove its children from the home but does not determine how the agency manages or concludes the complaint process.</p>
            <p>Where there is no protection concern and the complaint can be resolved without further involvement of protective services, all parties will seek to resolve the issue promptly and collaboratively.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="acknowledgement" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">schedule</i>
                <span class="card-title">Acknowledgement, Immediate Action, and Supports</span>
            </div>
            <p>Upon receipt of a complaint, the agency shall, within 24 hours:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>acknowledge receipt of the complaint to the complainant, verbally or in writing; acknowledgement happens even if no decision or action has yet occurred;</li>
                <li>document the complaint, including verbal complaints;</li>
                <li>assess whether any immediate action is required to protect the safety or well-being of the child; and</li>
                <li>determine what supports, if any, the complainant may require to meaningfully participate in the complaint review process.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Supports may include a trusted support person, advocacy assistance, or accommodations related to communication, developmental level, emotional needs, or cognitive capacity. The determination of supports shall be documented and reviewed as needed throughout the complaint process.</p>
            <p>Acknowledgement of a complaint shall occur even where further information gathering, investigation, or action is still underway.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="documentation" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">description</i>
                <span class="card-title">Documentation Requirements</span>
            </div>
            <p>Where a complaint relates to the care, treatment, or rights of a child or young person, the details of the complaint and the steps taken in response shall be documented in the child&rsquo;s file, including:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>the nature of the complaint;</li>
                <li>dates and timelines;</li>
                <li>individuals involved;</li>
                <li>actions taken and outcomes; and</li>
                <li>supports offered or provided.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Where applicable, a corresponding record may also be placed in the foster home file for oversight and cross-reference purposes.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="ombudsman" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">gavel</i>
                <span class="card-title">Ombudsman</span>
            </div>
            <p>A child experiencing foster care always has the right to speak in private and have visits with the Ontario Ombudsman when they have a complaint. They will be informed of this right on the date of placement in the foster home, during every plan of care, and as prescribed by the CYFSA. The review of the child&rsquo;s rights regarding the Ombudsman will be documented and signed by the child (or designated substitute consent provider) as well as the person who conducted the review. The child will also be made aware of resources provided by the Ombudsman to connect with other children experiencing foster care.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="processes" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">alt_route</i>
                <span class="card-title">Complaint Processes</span>
            </div>
            <p>The process followed depends on the source of the complaint.</p>
            <ul class="collapsible">
                <li class="active">
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="cm-proc-header-1" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="cm-proc-body-1">Complaint from the community regarding the foster home<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="cm-proc-body-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="cm-proc-header-1">
                        <p>Where a complaint is received from a community member:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>the placing agency shall receive and assess the complaint for severity and determine whether an investigation is required;</li>
                            <li>where an investigation is required, it shall commence within five (5) working days (see Investigation Procedures);</li>
                            <li>where no protection concern is identified, the placing agency shall contact the agency to discuss the complaint.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The agency shall:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>address the complaint with the foster home within 24 hours, either independently or in collaboration with the placing agency; and</li>
                            <li>document the complaint, actions taken, and outcome in the appropriate file(s).</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Where the agency receives the complaint directly:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>the agency shall notify the placing agency as soon as possible;</li>
                            <li>where a protection concern is identified, the appropriate placing agency shall be notified;</li>
                            <li>the complaint shall be addressed with the foster home within 24 hours; and</li>
                            <li>all actions and outcomes shall be documented in accordance with this policy.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="cm-proc-header-2" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cm-proc-body-2">Complaint from the placing agency regarding the foster home<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="cm-proc-body-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="cm-proc-header-2">
                        <p>Where a complaint is received from a placing agency:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>the placing agency shall communicate the complaint to the agency;</li>
                            <li>the agency shall assess the complaint and determine whether an investigation is required;</li>
                            <li>where an investigation is required, the Investigation Procedures shall be followed.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Where no investigation is required:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>the agency shall address the complaint with the foster home within 24 hours; and</li>
                            <li>the complaint, actions taken, and outcome shall be documented in accordance with this policy.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="cm-proc-header-3" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cm-proc-body-3">Complaint from a foster child regarding the foster home<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="cm-proc-body-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="cm-proc-header-3">
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>a child or young person may bring a complaint to any trusted person;</li>
                            <li>any person receiving the complaint shall ensure it is communicated to the agency as soon as possible;</li>
                            <li>contact information for agency personnel (e.g., Case Manager, Program Supervisor, Executive Director) shall be readily accessible to children.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The agency shall:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>notify the placing agency;</li>
                            <li>notify the appropriate CAS where a protection concern is identified;</li>
                            <li>assess any immediate safety concerns and determine supports required for the child to participate in the complaint process;</li>
                            <li>address the complaint with the foster home within 24 hours, where appropriate; and</li>
                            <li>document the complaint, actions taken, supports provided, and outcome in the child&rsquo;s file (with cross-reference to the foster home file, where applicable).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="review" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">fact_check</i>
                <span class="card-title">Review of a Complaint</span>
            </div>
            <p>Where applicable:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>the complainant shall receive a status update if requested;</li>
                <li>an initial status update shall be provided within 15 days of receipt of the complaint; and</li>
                <li>further updates shall be provided every 15 days until resolution.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The agency shall make all reasonable efforts to explain the outcome of the complaint in language appropriate to the complainant&rsquo;s age, maturity, and understanding.</p>
            <p>Where a child&rsquo;s rights have been violated, a review shall be conducted to develop or revise procedures to prevent recurrence.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="development" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">autorenew</i>
                <span class="card-title">Review and Continual Development</span>
            </div>
            <p>The agency shall review the effectiveness of the written complaints procedures and assess the need for any changes to improve outcomes. This review will be done within 12 months of the previous review.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="ministry" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">account_balance</i>
                <span class="card-title">Submission of Complaints to the Ministry</span>
            </div>
            <p>Current provincial regulations require the agency to submit a written analysis of every complaint on a monthly basis, no later than the 5th day of the following month, using the SOR-RL website. This submission will be conducted by the agency&rsquo;s Program Supervisor or a person whom the Program Supervisor designates on a temporary basis, such as a Director or Case Manager.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="debriefing" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">groups</i>
                <span class="card-title">Debriefing of a Complaint Outcome</span>
            </div>
            <p>The person or people who are related to the complaint must be debriefed. Once this has occurred, a second debriefing shall take place with the child who made the complaint or who is the subject of the complaint. During this debriefing, the child shall have an individual identified as a support person. These first two debriefings shall occur in the absence of other children.</p>
            <p>A final debriefing shall be offered to any children who witnessed any of the events related to the complaint.</p>
            <p>When debriefing children, accommodations must be made for their psychological, communication, and emotional needs, and cognitive capacity. The person conducting the debriefing shall make all reasonable efforts to understand the experiences of the child that led to the complaint and shall create a list of recommendations that the agency may adopt to mitigate the risk of similar events occurring.</p>
            <p>Debriefing shall occur within seven days of the complaint being reviewed. If circumstances prevent debriefing within this timeframe, the debriefing shall occur as soon as possible and the reason for the delay shall be documented, such as the child being away from the home or an ongoing child protection investigation.</p>
            <p>A record shall be kept of all debriefings and shall include:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>the names and titles, where applicable, of the persons being debriefed;</li>
                <li>the names and titles of the persons conducting the debriefings;</li>
                <li>the date, time, and duration of each debriefing; and</li>
                <li>the name of each child who was offered a debriefing and whether they attended or declined.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="notifications" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">notifications_active</i>
                <span class="card-title">Required Notifications</span>
            </div>
            <p>Following receipt and review of a complaint, the agency shall ensure that all required notifications are completed and documented. Where a complaint is made by or regarding a child, the following shall apply:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>when a child is not placed under an Extended Society Care status, the parent or legal guardian of the child shall be notified of any complaints made by or regarding that child;</li>
                <li>in all cases, the placing agency or society that placed the child shall be notified;</li>
                <li>where a complaint involves or gives rise to child protection concerns, the appropriate Children&rsquo;s Aid Society shall be notified in accordance with applicable legislation and protocols; and</li>
                <li>where a complaint meets the criteria for a Serious Occurrence, it shall be logged in the Ministry&rsquo;s SOR-RL online platform in accordance with Serious Occurrence Reporting requirements.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The agency shall also ensure that:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>the complainant is notified when the complaint review is concluded; and</li>
                <li>the outcome is explained in a manner appropriate to the complainant&rsquo;s age, maturity, and understanding.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Documentation confirming that all required notifications have been completed shall be retained in the appropriate file.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

